    "notes": "ONE part \"Voice\", one staff, pickup + 10 measures of 3/4 on 2 systems. THREE verses under the staff, numbered \"1.\"-\"3.\" (Latin, Italian, Spanish). 11 lyric elisions: two syllables sung on one note and joined by an undertie (a~in, et~in, ta~e, da~il, ta~an, ra~u, ce~e, ta~y, ba~al, ta~o, y~el); each must stay ONE lyric on ONE note (MusicXML <text>a</text><elision/><text>in</text>), not two notes or two lyrics. Two slurred melismas per verse (extender or hyphen), non-ASCII syllables in verse 3 (Se-ñor, co-ra-zón)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Elided syllables are one <lyric> with <syllabic>/<text> pairs separated by <elision>‿</elision>; the first part keeps the hyphen to the previous syllable, the last part the hyphen to the next.",
